] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831e7e0a-aed0-5ddf-b0ff-b8a7a383aa33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375120} {:answer/id #uuid "2c195dd0-eb81-5875-976a-a093838b8853" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375121} {:answer/id #uuid "6626a63d-9e1d-5478-a4a4-2f51d2d4d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375122} {:answer/id #uuid "9853f3f2-3c76-59b2-a379-62cf6f71ab60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375123} {:answer/id #uuid "36d84cc3-78f8-5a9d-ae00-dd3d24948008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6626a63d-9e1d-5478-a4a4-2f51d2d4d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375122} :answer-field/id #uuid "60f91179-c02c-52de-821c-db603b09c9de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0a05944-cd54-5fbe-bad9-a47ce86875e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73738" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-2+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=⟨-2+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67ce3d47-3a84-5e17-90b5-808e763e7600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375127} {:answer/id #uuid "75c1aea2-3b43-5433-afdd-3342b9b8199d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375128} {:answer/id #uuid "f19c4b5d-373e-56d0-a2d5-a2f69be406d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375129} {:answer/id #uuid "e9026196-05ec-500e-9e73-bcb561d459d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375130} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cd479c-433f-5017-89d7-3a080859c4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ce3d47-3a84-5e17-90b5-808e763e7600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375127} :answer-field/id #uuid "38efa2d1-90b7-5a8e-b8f2-28ae7d0ce4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73740" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07f2ae4c-ff07-5b99-a7b0-90f460081eef" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Singular 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbfd7428-1d1d-5ad8-8054-e1349712bb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375134} {:answer/id #uuid "f915a012-6351-5d0d-ba7a-0b98a70a6a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375135} {:answer/id #uuid "f95f3d05-0823-54d3-9f52-27fd855eef25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375136} {:answer/id #uuid "2e2e79a8-0e70-5741-b9be-f622b3aa6697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375137} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2da10a-189d-5939-bcce-517cbd6aec24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbfd7428-1d1d-5ad8-8054-e1349712bb03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375134} :answer-field/id #uuid "834515f8-6272-5827-bfac-7bf41c342fd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79d64547-fc54-5cd3-a6ec-b00c0e085729" :question/math-academy-id "q-73750" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ -3x+6y=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=4 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=4.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
